{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545484-what-are-your-least-favorite-paths","id":1545484,"title":"What are your least favorite Paths?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-06T12:16:37-08:00","id":1545484,"title":"What are your least favorite Paths?","content":"I'm not to much of a Path of Enlightenment or Road fan and stick with humanity all the time.<br /> <br /> So I'm curious what were the worst ideas for a path/road that you saw for the game?<br /> <br /> Myself I read the description for Path of Harmony and it seems like a very hard and at times lonely path to walk and easy to justify horrible actions when caught up in an act of passion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 11-06-2024, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T14:58:03-08:00","id":1545493,"title":"","content":"Cathari. It doesn't feel like a viable way of behaving. I got so irritated with that path that I made it a plot-point to have them nearly destroy the Sabbat, and then get declared heretical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T18:15:52-08:00","id":1545503,"title":"","content":"I'm going to diverge a bit from the question because I tend not to have too strong of opinions about specific Paths given how many implementations have happened over the years that have had me waffle on my least favorites. I'm going to go over what annoys me broadly:<br /> <br /> 1) Mono-Clan appeal. Paths, and even more-so Roads, work best as an additional minor social stratus in the game. It's another bit of politics you can add to the game on top of Sect and Clan conflicts. When a Path/Road really only exists for one Clan, it's just internal Clan politics with more rules. I will say I mean this more OOC, there are Paths/Roads heavily associated with one Clan, but really could appeal to a much wider group of vampires and there's no real reason in-universe why it hasn't (which is its own story hook to make more interesting).<br /> <br /> 2) While very frustrating terminology, when DAV originally developed the Roads, they gave each Road a selection of Paths (like that's not confusing...). The idea was that each Road, as a broad philosophy, had a number of sub-roads (to which path is a decent word) to handle different approaches. These weren't mechanical changes (even if it's clear that some were meant to develop into modern nights fully independent Paths over time), just interesting ways to make things more variable. What does it look like to be on the Road of Kings if you're not the King? Well the paths gave options for that. Even without the formal designation DAV gave, I think the worst Paths are the most restrictive to ideological variation. Again, I give a bit of leeway if the books have multiple Paths that are supposed to be offshoots of the same thing (Beast gets the most of this), but you should be able to have debates between members of the Path on moral/ethical issues, and a lot of them really don't allow it in favor of very uniform members just out of what the Path entails.<br /> <br /> 3) Major inconsistency between the descriptions of the Path (esp. the Path ethics sections) and the mechanics of the Path (the actual hierarchy and Virtues). Instinct is frequently a bad sign to me given what Instinct does differently mechanically, and how little sense it can make with give Paths. One of the worst examples if probably the idea that Metamorphosis uses Instinct despite being portrayed as a more scholarly Road/Path that's out to explore the boundaries of vampirism and shatter them. The ethics and Hierarchy talk about acts they control and unleash the Beast... something Instinct doesn't really do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T09:42:13-08:00","id":1545524,"title":"","content":"Well... I mostly agree with the previous comments here<br /> <br /> And to me, Roads inside the Paths was just more content padding to fill more suplementary books. While I do like the Road Books, they ended up having that 'fill all slots in the most formulaic way possible'. Like, there is a lot of Roads of Kings, which should just be 'take hierarchy and promises seriously'. If I had to choose one, I'd say Road of Merchants, which for me is stupid. But Road of Tyrants is even worst. If you want a Road of do whatever I want, have the balls to go Road of Sin dammit<br /> <br /> Road of Paradox has a lot of interesting ideas. The whole concept of you having to keep zero kharma dept and fulfill both your destiny and not interfere into others I think is awesome. But all the one-off specific Sins, like 'don't embrace women' or 'go bother those who seek golconda' feels stupid. <br /> Path of Typhoon feels similar a lot of the time. <br /> <br /> But, in a way I never liked the system of Paths in Vampire. It basically forced the ST to keep in mind a list of 5-7 triggers of Sin, for every PC that followed a damn Path, besides the one of Humanity itself. It also wasn't clear if you rolled a single time for like each Sin or only the sum of all the Sin in that Scene. The difference between the base Virtues and the alternatives wasn't good either. I love the idea of Paths, but the system never gelled with me. And the Aura thing? also cool in concept, but just more babble to keep remembering and taking account.<br /> <br /> While there isn't an official Paths system in V5, I much prefer how the integrity (Humanity) works, and it wasn't hard to make a homebrew Path system over it. It was more converting them into V5 than anything else. Of course, homebrew is never a good solution, these thing should be solved officialy, but how much better it works, for me, makes it uncomparable with the janky original system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T21:07:45-08:00","id":1545549,"title":"","content":"I'd say that the Road/Path of the Hive and anything connected with the Baali gets a negative from me.<br /> <br /> This may sound pretentious but I hope you'll survive it.<br /> <br /> There are a Paths I find lacking in, shall we say, philosophical basis like the Path of the Merchant but I'm kind of cool with most Roads and Paths. The main thing for me is that they should be about an outlook on Cainite existance which can promote a certain lifestyle, or have some kind of existential question that its based around. But it shouldn't be only about a lifestyle. Cainites who are not inclined to philosophy should simply have a lower rating on their Road and not pursue its tenants all to fiercely.<br /> <br /> Just like many Camarilla Cainites don't seem to care all that much about the philosophical parts or be to be a paragon of Humanity, even if they are on Humanity. Thus I find that a worldy merchant unconcerned with philosophy should just get along with his trading business on a lower Road rating but with more freedom of action from committing a sin, rather, than having a specific Path for being a Merchant.<br /> <br /> Or at least that's my view and I will confess it was some time since I took a look in the &quot;Road of Kings&quot; book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T22:37:00-08:00","id":1545553,"title":"","content":"Not so much honerable accord but the idea circulating the community and some game designers that its 'nice', humanity ajacant or even particulary respectable. This is an incredably naive outlook if you consider what is permitted or rather explicitly not excluded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T22:41:07-08:00","id":1545554,"title":"","content":"Precisely as each society has it own views on what is considered honorable behavior and while there might be some common themes. It's not a given that each kindred would have the same take on the path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T23:06:53-08:00","id":1545559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545484-what-are-your-least-favorite-paths?p=1545554#post1545554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Precisely as each society has it own views on what is considered honorable behavior and while there might be some common themes. It's not a given that each kindred would have the same take on the path.</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote someone else about it &quot;my arcane code of conduct says nothing about rape, innocents or mercy and making an example for stepping out of line is completly acceptable for killing&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-08-2024, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T23:35:33-08:00","id":1545562,"title":"","content":"So, Path of the Hive is one of the ones I waffle on... which is funny because I've completely cut it out of my games anyway. As a Path... it's towards the bottom of my list at any given moment, but I just don't like the implications of the Baali to their themes and role in the setting. Something I found highly rewarding for helping make the Baali deeper antagonists (but not less irredeemably evil) was stealing the Autonomy trait from WtA Revised's Possessed book. Basically, the idea was to have the Baali get out of the &quot;code of ethics to bind the Beast&quot; game completely by trading their souls to demonic forces and getting an internal demonic entity instead of the normal vampire beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-08T11:36:29-08:00","id":1545578,"title":"","content":"Something tells me that the Baali are closer to Caine essence then the rest of the clans. The great knowledge, but without any real wisdom to back it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T15:03:16-08:00","id":1545817,"title":"","content":"I'm a V:tM Grognard when it comes to paths; Humanity is the only one for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T11:53:10-08:00","id":1545865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545484-what-are-your-least-favorite-paths?p=1545559#post1545559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To quote someone else about it &quot;my arcane code of conduct says nothing about rape, innocents or mercy and making an example for stepping out of line is completly acceptable for killing&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there can be a lot of assumed chivalry in the Path of Honorable Accord, but it could not necessarily be the case. Bushido has a code of conduct, but it didn't prevent a lot of atrocities in either the Sengoku Jidai or World War II by its adherents. When you consider that Honorable Accord is a Sabbat path designed to protect the sect (and seemingly the Sabbat's elders), it's a problem.<br /> <br /> I think one major problem with a lot of Paths is that people forget the Path to constrain the Beast. The Path does not only need to be internally consistent, but always putting the vampire in a place to tell the Beast &quot;no&quot;. No, I am not going to feed right now. No, I am not going to kill this other person. No, I am not going to eliminate this potential threat. No, I am not going to be sadistic or whatever it is the Beast wants me to do. Because if it doesn't do that, then the Beast is going to take over through the obvious exceptions (making it a failed Path). (The idea that some Paths control the Beast by satiating it so it doesn't act in when it would be inconvenient for the vampire is an interesting idea, but I don't think it works in practice.)<br /> <br /> That the Revised era Path of Honorable Accord is based on Conscience (and Self-Control) indicates the Path is supposed to be humane in some capacity and cover things other than just &quot;being honorable&quot;. It requires a person to have a developed moral conscience and not violate it as well. But the original Path of Honorable Accord used Callousness, Instincts, and Morale just like every other Sabbat Path meaning it is not more humane than the other Paths.<br /> <br /> I figure that there are probably variants of Honorable Accord. One, a moral one somewhat comparable to Humanity, that does integrate a moral conscience with the concept of honor, and then a second based on Conviction that allows more monstrous conduct, though still honorable conduct (in the style of &quot;honorable villains&quot; that are popular in media).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T12:12:52-08:00","id":1545867,"title":"","content":"While a bit of a retcon since the Sabbat Paths came first, I always figured DAV's take is that the Path of Honorable Accord is part of the Road of Kings family of Paths that took the Chivalry part of Road of Kings and adapted it to the Sabbat's needs. It's not like it's a big stretch... chivalry as practiced in reality was, like Bushido, not something that started as some noble code of righteous action. Both were cultural teachings meant to keep a military class under the thumb of the ruling class but socially superior to the other classes in society with broad range to treat their &quot;inferiors&quot; with little regard. Knights and samurai both got a lot of historical revisionism to paint them as much better people to justify their continued power in society despite the need for a landed gentry warrior class disappearing.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure there needs to be two different versions, or that you need a Conviction version to be a brutal warrior. Conscience works fine for applying force incorrectly as a shameful act even if your views of what kinds of force are acceptable is wildly out of step with Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-18T03:52:00-08:00","id":1546070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545484-what-are-your-least-favorite-paths?p=1545867#post1545867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a bit of a retcon since the Sabbat Paths came first, I always figured DAV's take is that the Path of Honorable Accord is part of the Road of Kings family of Paths that took the Chivalry part of Road of Kings and adapted it to the Sabbat's needs. It's not like it's a big stretch... chivalry as practiced in reality was, like Bushido, not something that started as some noble code of righteous action. Both were cultural teachings meant to keep a military class under the thumb of the ruling class but socially superior to the other classes in society with broad range to treat their &quot;inferiors&quot; with little regard. Knights and samurai both got a lot of historical revisionism to paint them as much better people to justify their continued power in society despite the need for a landed gentry warrior class disappearing.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure there needs to be two different versions, or that you need a Conviction version to be a brutal warrior. Conscience works fine for applying force incorrectly as a shameful act even if your views of what kinds of force are acceptable is wildly out of step with Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, you're 100% correct but I also think may be running past the point.<br /> <br /> Basically, Bushido and the Code of Chivalry existed essentially in order to try to reign in the natural state of the warrior, which is of course that you kill people for your profession. It was always observed in violation more than obedience because that's why the codes existed in the first place. Sort of like how Christianity has a bunch of rules that get violated because, yes, the purpose is the rules to tell people not to do X in the first place.<br /> <br /> Or TLDR, &quot;A proper chivalric knight would be a 10 on the Road of Kings but very rarely would your typical knight reach that anymore than a human reaches Humanity 10.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-20T14:02:40-08:00","id":1546210,"title":"","content":"To quote Chris Hedges is that these are ideals to aspire to and do the best you can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-20T17:37:45-08:00","id":1546223,"title":"","content":"It's not so much a matter of paths I dislike, but rather a problem in the way many were structured.<br /> <br /> To me, the gold standard is the way humanity is done. You have at the bottom the most morality breaking acts and also the most difficult to accomplish, it's not everyday your average humanity based kindred will go on a genocide.<br /> <br /> And the highest the humanity, the more difficult it is to hold. To the point where humanity 10 is about even avoiding having thoughts of harming others.<br /> <br /> Which makes a good model for paths. The lower ratings should enforce the core of the philosophy with the level 1 sins being an utter betrayal of the beliefs, and the higher one is on their path, the more abstract and hard to maintain.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, many paths falls short of that, and it sometimes feels like a much needed rework would have helped.<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's take three paths that falls short of this standard, but are in their concepts amongs my favorites.<br /> <br /> The path of power and the inner voice is basically making the average machiavellian elder tendances into a philosophy.<br /> <br /> The level 1 sin is not taking power or advantage when you have the occasion.<br /> So far so good, that's the core of the path, so it's expected that it would be the level 1.<br /> <br /> But then we have the level 7 sin, which is helping others without gaining an advantage by doing so. And the rationale is that you should always take advantage by your actions.<br /> <br /> Which is.... Exactly level 1?<br /> <br /> This one looks like the writers had trouble finding 10 specific sins for that path<br /> <br /> The we have the path of death and the soul<br /> <br /> So extreme scholarship focused on death. But the priorities of the sins are all messed up<br /> <br /> The level 1 sin is not letting a death happening<br /> But level 5 is not pursuing enlightenment. By all account, enlightenment is the core oft he path and breaking it should be the level 1 sin<br /> <br /> Same problem with one of my favorite path, at least in concept, metamorphosis.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bNow the path makes the capital sin (sorry for the pun) of being borderline unplayable due to it's weird focus on not caring about others.<br /> <br /> To the point that showing compassion (and here we have the vague sin, does it means to have compassion or to show compassionate behavior, the second that may be manipulation?)<br /> <br /> How is that the deal breaker of this path?<br /> <br /> In the same way, why is &quot;postponing feeding when hungry&quot; so high on the list when it's a pretty easy situation to deal with?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> By all logic, the level 1 sin should be the actual level 4 sin of &quot;not modifying yourself when you have the chance.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bTldr: many paths needs to have their order of sins reworked<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 11-20-2024, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-21T03:14:10-08:00","id":1546233,"title":"","content":"I've never used paths, so I can only give my opinion based on what I've read. I think they're good conceptually, but using them in practice seems to be more of a hassle than they're worth. In the end, I think they work more as a reference than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-21T09:34:12-08:00","id":1546246,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think the whole system of 10 Sins is terrible for many reasons. It was okay-ish when it came out in 1991, it was innovative as concept, and it was easier to manage since all PCs used the same list of Sins, with varying degrees.<br /> <br /> But Paths? The ST gotta know every Sin the PC is over in their particular Path, and remember the Virtue associated, and it becomes a mess. <br /> The Ethics described in each Path are 4 out of 5 times, the best descriptions and Sins-Virtues of the Path. So they really should've used those as the basis for the gameplay, not an increasing list of 10 Sins, that become awfully cumbersome to remember at all times. Besides, some Sins are awfully described, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> said, you don't know if it is spirit or in action, if it is to other or yourself; and the order of some is confusing. <br /> <br /> Much better if there were only 5 sins-virtues, working like Convictions to each Path. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also. Some Paths seem to be told very differently depending on each author and book, and the memo on some seem to be forgotten when some recurrent characters are written in novels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-21T11:24:21-08:00","id":1546249,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem with the game design of the Paths is that Humanity is an excellent example of how early VtM was innovative but also not refined. The WoD's struggle between being a highly thematic storytelling game, and a verisimilitude enabling reality emulator has never really be resolved. Humanity (and from it the Paths) is, through many revisions still, a hard to handle mix of both concepts that end up butting heads more than reinforcing each other.<br /> <br /> That is basically the origin of Paths: they did start as a &quot;reference&quot; because the Sabbat needed to be monstrous in their rejection of Humanity, but functional antagonists that could operate as plotting scheming vampires even while regularly performing acts that would drop them to Humanity 0 and having no interest in &quot;repenting&quot; to regain Humanity just to lose it again. So the thematic side of Humanity as a doom spiral of moral compromises has to share space with a system that replicates characters with differing moral codes because even among real world humans Humanity is far from a universal fit for how people would rank &quot;sins&quot; so why should vampires have a single locked in objective moral philosophy? As the Sabbat expanded - they were made playable fairly quickly in the scheme of things compared to other antagonists like the Technocracy - the tug of war between &quot;ways to chain the Beast to avoid falling into being a mindless monster&quot; and &quot;ways to represent the diversity of vampire moral philosophy&quot; continued to wage.<br /> <br /> Most of the best fixes to this fundamental issue with the concept of Humanity and Paths, are ones that either side with one part of the intentions over the other, or split them up into multiple places so it's easier for each goal to have a place.<br /> <br /> For example, I fairly decent homebrew I saw once scrapped Humanity and Paths as implemented and swapped in CofD 2e's Intergrity with Path Ethics replacing the character questionnaire in CofD and Path auras staying to handle the verisimilitude aspect. Then they adapted the VtR 1e Atrocity dice to handle the moral doom spiral of being a vampire. Up-keeping a high &quot;Humanity-but-really-Integrity&quot; meant auras (and thus Paths can be very unsettling), and a small bonus when dealing with Atrocity dice, but Atrocity hits everyone the same regardless of what moral codes they try to follow.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this to promote a specific house-rule, but to illustrate that decoupling some of the important things Humanity/Paths bring to the game into two or three different elements instead can let each shine more effectively than cramming them all in one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-21T20:28:18-08:00","id":1546273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545484-what-are-your-least-favorite-paths?p=1546249#post1546249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is basically the origin of Paths: they did start as a &quot;reference&quot; because the Sabbat needed to be monstrous in their rejection of Humanity, but functional antagonists that could operate as plotting scheming vampires even while regularly performing acts that would drop them to Humanity 0 and having no interest in &quot;repenting&quot; to regain Humanity just to lose it again. So the thematic side of Humanity as a doom spiral of moral compromises has to share space with a system that replicates characters with differing moral codes because even among real world humans Humanity is far from a universal fit for how people would rank &quot;sins&quot; so why should vampires have a single locked in objective moral philosophy? As the Sabbat expanded - they were made playable fairly quickly in the scheme of things compared to other antagonists like the Technocracy - the tug of war between &quot;ways to chain the Beast to avoid falling into being a mindless monster&quot; and &quot;ways to represent the diversity of vampire moral philosophy&quot; continued to wage.<br /> .<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a fair point, it's true that quite a lot of paths seems more like a codified philosophy rather than a reaction to the beast.<br /> <br /> To quote those I listed above, neither death and the soul or power and the inner voice seems to care about the beast. And metamorphosis only mention it as in one should learn from both fighting and accepting it.<br /> <br /> <br /> It would make sense that most of them should be considered philosophies rather than code of ethics. For exemple, seeing the empasis of metamorphosists on evolution of both flesh and mind, one would expect than rather tha' being a path of itself, they would alternate between various paths across their un life. <br /> <br /> Same for death and soul. It doesn't tell you anything about the beast, it's just a study of death and a relationship with mortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 11-21-2024, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-22T20:33:54-08:00","id":1546297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545484-what-are-your-least-favorite-paths?p=1546273#post1546273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's a fair point, it's true that quite a lot of paths seems more like a codified philosophy rather than a reaction to the beast.<br /> <br /> To quote those I listed above, neither death and the soul or power and the inner voice seems to care about the beast. And metamorphosis only mention it as in one should learn from both fighting and accepting it.<br /> <br /> <br /> It would make sense that most of them should be considered philosophies rather than code of ethics. For exemple, seeing the empasis of metamorphosists on evolution of both flesh and mind, one would expect than rather tha' being a path of itself, they would alternate between various paths across their un life.<br /> <br /> Same for death and soul. It doesn't tell you anything about the beast, it's just a study of death and a relationship with mortality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think the premise for Paths as ways to have monstrous vampires who aren't half a step from turning into a Wight was okay, but the mechanics are a bit wonky, and some Paths especially don't feel like they fit within the Vampire concept, due to stuff like simply not even mentioning the Beast (which is the ultimate purpose of a Path - a way to avoid falling to the Beast).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T08:55:27-08:00","id":1546388,"title":"","content":"I have the privilege of having played with some great players at healthy tables, who took roads and paths seriously and played characters true to them when applicable. I've also played with less-skilled and poorly-intended players, so I see all sides of the argument. Paths/roads in general are a net benefit to the game, when taken seriously and played well; when not, it's entirely valid to not appreciate them as a player or an ST. So that said, the paths and roads I view as problematic aren't necessarily the ones that are difficult to comprehend or play, but rather those with the most leeway for abuse. You know, the &quot;paths of what I was going to do anyway&quot;.<br /> <br /> Atop that list for me are the OG versions of Typhon and Paradox, which were essentially the &quot;Paths of Being an Asshole Player&quot;. Other problematic paths can still be played well without wreaking havoc at a table to whatever end, but Typhon and Paradox mandate disruptive gameplay. It absolutely doesn't help those two paths are specific to clans to which problematic players gravitate. Granted later iterations of the paths have been fixed for the most part, but the older versions still stand as the best examples of how paths can and do go wrong.<br /> <br /> Special note here go to paths like Power and the Inner Voice, and Caine, which either tacitly or explicitly condone diablerie. Diablerie isn't the only potential issue with the paths; it just happens to be the most obvious and illustrative problematic use case. Those paths can still be played well and compelling personal narratives built around them, but they definitely need to be handled with care by players and ST's lest the potential for using those paths as an excuse for playing disruptively come to the forefront.<br /> <br /> I do agree with others the &quot;one sin per level in ascending order&quot; regime has always had its share of issues. In that, even Humanity is no different -- vandalism being a level 5 sin more or less says it all. Especially when that level 5 sin is neatly crouched between two nebulously-defined and contradicting degrees of manslaughter.<br /> <br /> For example, is draining a mortal while in hunger frenzy a level 4 or 6 sin? Level 6 specifies starvation (the trigger for hunger frenzy, it's right there in the name), but level 4 specifies frenzy for which hunger frenzy is one form (again, right there in the name). The implication is it's a lower-order sin for a vampire to resist frenzy but go too far feeding from a mortal regardless, than it is to lose control of oneself. Granted that's kind of a straw man example as specific overrides general, and no storyteller of which I'm aware would rule draining a mortal in hunger frenzy a level 4 opposed to 6 sin, but it still serves well to point out the contradictions and ill definition present in even the game's default path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T15:31:01-08:00","id":1546409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545484-what-are-your-least-favorite-paths?p=1546388#post1546388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Atop that list for me are the OG versions of Typhon and Paradox, which were essentially the &quot;Paths of Being an Asshole Player&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially as originally written, I think the Setites and Ravnos (and in fact all the non-Camarilla 7 clans) were intended primarily to be antagonists, so Paths that lead themselves to being antagonists aren't a problem for the setting per se. They justified why characters of those clans would be antagonists. But they are a problem when a player wants to play one in a game cooperating with other players. It's like running an RPG set in World War II and everyone makes Allied characters and one player insists on playing a Nazi just because its technically an option in the rulebook.<br /> <br /> One of the big differences between 1e/2e and Revised is that the earlier depictions tried to present a holistic setting where some potential character choices simply were not ideal from a gaming group perspective, and the other wanted to make everything much more playable. The difference between the Setites of these versions is just irreconcilable. Unless you were playing a Setite who was trying to escape the cult in 1e/2e, the Setites were just going to be assholes. Perfectly fine choice as a setting element, but it did limit their playability in any generic gaming group.<br /> <br /> Now even those antagonistic choices could still be playable given the right players, coterie concept, and chronicle, but it requires more coordination and maturity than most standard games (which is typically everyone creates their own character, and everyone hopes it all works out together as a group).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T13:21:56-08:00","id":1546990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545484-what-are-your-least-favorite-paths?p=1546249#post1546249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem with the game design of the Paths is that Humanity is an excellent example of how early VtM was innovative but also not refined. The WoD's struggle between being a highly thematic storytelling game, and a verisimilitude enabling reality emulator has never really be resolved. Humanity (and from it the Paths) is, through many revisions still, a hard to handle mix of both concepts that end up butting heads more than reinforcing each other.<br /> <br /> That is basically the origin of Paths: they did start as a &quot;reference&quot; because the Sabbat needed to be monstrous in their rejection of Humanity, but functional antagonists that could operate as plotting scheming vampires even while regularly performing acts that would drop them to Humanity 0 and having no interest in &quot;repenting&quot; to regain Humanity just to lose it again. So the thematic side of Humanity as a doom spiral of moral compromises has to share space with a system that replicates characters with differing moral codes because even among real world humans Humanity is far from a universal fit for how people would rank &quot;sins&quot; so why should vampires have a single locked in objective moral philosophy? As the Sabbat expanded - they were made playable fairly quickly in the scheme of things compared to other antagonists like the Technocracy - the tug of war between &quot;ways to chain the Beast to avoid falling into being a mindless monster&quot; and &quot;ways to represent the diversity of vampire moral philosophy&quot; continued to wage.<br /> <br /> Most of the best fixes to this fundamental issue with the concept of Humanity and Paths, are ones that either side with one part of the intentions over the other, or split them up into multiple places so it's easier for each goal to have a place.<br /> <br /> For example, I fairly decent homebrew I saw once scrapped Humanity and Paths as implemented and swapped in CofD 2e's Intergrity with Path Ethics replacing the character questionnaire in CofD and Path auras staying to handle the verisimilitude aspect. Then they adapted the VtR 1e Atrocity dice to handle the moral doom spiral of being a vampire. Up-keeping a high &quot;Humanity-but-really-Integrity&quot; meant auras (and thus Paths can be very unsettling), and a small bonus when dealing with Atrocity dice, but Atrocity hits everyone the same regardless of what moral codes they try to follow.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this to promote a specific house-rule, but to illustrate that decoupling some of the important things Humanity/Paths bring to the game into two or three different elements instead can let each shine more effectively than cramming them all in one.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds interesting. Please share if you have the homebrew to hand!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T13:43:13-08:00","id":1546992,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately I can't seem to find it in my shared-with-you Google files... but it's been a long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}